{
  "answer": "Remote HTTP MCP servers that authorize MUST speak RFC 9728 PRM, 401+WWW-Authenticate, and RFC 8707 resource indicators; clients MUST send Bearer tokens in the Authorization header, never the query string. STDIO is exempt and uses the environment. Official Python and TypeScript SDKs implement the HTTP flow in captured source. MCP Inspector CLI cliOAuth.ts is PARTIAL-OR-ABSENT for PKCE/PRM in that file (callback wiring only). This program does not ship that HTTP client; its MCP surface is STDIO .mcp.json. A hop-by-hop location trace of the HTTP flow plus a scan of this artifact show the artifact is credential-free. SUCCESS:RES-0044 in the receipt AND a hop-by-hop token-location trace plus a scan result showing the artifact is credential-free",
